WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.429 --> 00:00:04.569
Dear Fellow Scholars, this is Two Minute Papers
with Károly Zsolnai-Fehér.

00:00:04.569 --> 00:00:11.120
In 2017, scientists at OpenAI embarked on
an AI project where they wanted to show a

00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:17.100
neural network a bunch of Amazon product reviews
and wanted to teach it to be able to generate

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:20.970
new ones, or continue a review when given
one.

00:00:20.970 --> 00:00:26.480
Now, so far, this sounds like a nice hobby
project, definitely not something that would

00:00:26.480 --> 00:00:33.380
justify an entire video on this channel, however,
during this experiment, something really unexpected

00:00:33.380 --> 00:00:34.380
happened.

00:00:34.380 --> 00:00:39.420
Now, it is clear that when the neural network
reads these reviews, it knows that it has

00:00:39.420 --> 00:00:44.460
to generate new ones, therefore it builds
up a deep understanding of language.

00:00:44.460 --> 00:00:50.190
However, beyond that, it used surprisingly
few neurons to continue these reviews and

00:00:50.190 --> 00:00:53.530
scientists were wondering “why is that”?

00:00:53.530 --> 00:01:00.210
Usually, the more neurons, the more powerful
the AI can get, so why use so few neurons?

00:01:00.210 --> 00:01:03.590
The reason for that is that it has learned
something really interesting.

00:01:03.590 --> 00:01:05.860
I’ll tell you what in a moment.

00:01:05.860 --> 00:01:11.140
This neural network was trained in an unsupervised
manner, therefore it was told to do what the

00:01:11.140 --> 00:01:14.869
task was, but was given no further supervision.

00:01:14.869 --> 00:01:18.700
No labeled datasets, no additional help, nothing.

00:01:18.700 --> 00:01:23.549
Upon closer inspection, they noticed that
the neural network has built up a knowledge

00:01:23.549 --> 00:01:28.420
of not only language, but also built a sentiment
detector as well.

00:01:28.420 --> 00:01:33.010
This means that the AI recognized that in
order to be able to continue a review, it

00:01:33.010 --> 00:01:38.530
needs to be able to efficiently detect whether
the review seems positive or not.

00:01:38.530 --> 00:01:44.229
And thus, it dedicated a neuron to this task,
which we will refer to as the sentiment neuron.

00:01:44.229 --> 00:01:50.240
However, it was no ordinary sentiment neuron,
it was a proper, state of the art sentiment

00:01:50.240 --> 00:01:51.380
detector.

00:01:51.380 --> 00:01:54.090
In this diagram, you see this neuron at work.

00:01:54.090 --> 00:01:58.610
As it reads through the review, it starts
out detecting a positive outlook which you

00:01:58.610 --> 00:02:05.920
can see with green, and then, uh-oh, it detects
that review has taken a turn and is not happy

00:02:05.920 --> 00:02:07.600
with the movie at all.

00:02:07.600 --> 00:02:11.049
And all this was learned on a relatively small
dataset.

00:02:11.049 --> 00:02:15.560
Now, if we have this sentiment neuron, we
don’t just have to sit around and be happy

00:02:15.560 --> 00:02:16.560
for it.

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:17.790
Let’s play with it!

00:02:17.790 --> 00:02:22.900
For instance, by overwriting this sentiment
neuron in the neural network, we can force

00:02:22.900 --> 00:02:26.629
it to create positive or negative reviews.

00:02:26.629 --> 00:02:30.939
Here is a positive example: “Just what I
was looking for.

00:02:30.939 --> 00:02:36.530
Nice fitted pants, exactly matched seam to
color contrast with other pants I own.

00:02:36.530 --> 00:02:39.389
Highly recommended and also very happy!”

00:02:39.389 --> 00:02:45.360
And, if we overwrite the sentiment neuron
to negative, we get the following: “The

00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:48.099
package received was blank and has no barcode.

00:02:48.099 --> 00:02:49.720
A waste of time and money.”

00:02:49.720 --> 00:02:53.150
There are some more examples here on the screen
for your pleasure.

00:02:53.150 --> 00:02:54.150
Absolutely amazing.

00:02:54.150 --> 00:02:59.290
This paper teaches us that we should endeavor
to not just accept these AI-based solutions,

00:02:59.290 --> 00:03:06.540
but look under the hood, and sometimes, a
goldmine of knowledge can be found within.

